:Namespace test_Core
⍝ Core JSON and REST request-handling tests for Jarvis
⍝ Usage:
⍝   From the shell (repository root):  dyalogscript Tests/Core/run.apls
⍝   From an APL session with #.Jarvis loaded:  #.test_Core.Run
⍝ Run returns a vector of failure messages; empty means every test passed.
⍝ Each test starts its own Jarvis on its own port and drives it with a raw Conga client (Jarvis's own LDRC),
⍝ sending complete HTTP requests with "Connection: close" so the whole response can be read back.
⍝ Ports: BasePort+1, BasePort+2, ... (8391 and up by default). Set BasePort before Run, or JARVIS_TEST_PORT for run.apls.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1
    CRLF←⎕UCS 13 10
    BasePort←8390
    Verbose←1

    TJarvisSource←':Class TJarvis: #.Jarvis' ':Field Public Logged←⍬' '∇ {msg}←{level}Log msg' ':Access public override' 'Logged,←⊂,⍕msg' '∇' ':EndClass'

    ∇ r←Run;tests;t;res
      :Access public
      r←⍬
      :If 9≠#.⎕NC'Jarvis'
          →0⊣r←,⊂'#.Jarvis is not loaded'
      :EndIf
      ⎕FIX TJarvisSource
      tests←{⍵/⍨'test_'∘≡¨5↑¨⍵}⎕NL ¯3
      PortsUsed←0
      :For t :In tests
          App←MakeApp
          (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
          :Trap 0
              res←⍎t
          :Else
              res←,⊂'errored: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM
          :EndTrap
          StopAll
          r,←(⊂t,': '),¨res
          :If Verbose
              ⎕←t,': ',(1+0∊⍴res)⊃('FAILED (',(⍕≢res),')')'passed'
              ⎕←⍪res
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
    ∇

⍝ ─── the application code (CodeLocation) used by the tests ─────────────────────────

    ∇ app←MakeApp
      app←⎕NS''
      app.Inited←0 ⋄ app.ClosedFlag←0
    ⍝ JSON endpoints
      app.⎕FX'r←echo p' 'r←p'                        ⍝ round-trips the payload
      app.⎕FX'r←add p' 'r←+/p'                        ⍝ numeric
      app.⎕FX'r←req withreq p;n' 'n←⎕NS''''' 'n.(method sum)←req.Method(+/p)' 'r←n' ⍝ ambivalent: req as ⍺
      app.⎕FX'r←boom p' 'r←÷0'                         ⍝ errors → 500
      app.⎕FX'r←secret p' 'r←''SECRET'''              ⍝ for Include/Exclude
    ⍝ hooks
      app.⎕FX'r←Init srv' 'Inited←1' 'r←0'            ⍝ AppInitFn
      app.⎕FX'r←Closed' 'ClosedFlag←1' 'r←0'          ⍝ AppCloseFn (niladic, result-returning)
      app.⎕FX'r←Validate req' 'r←''block''≡req.GetHeader''x-validate''' ⍝ ValidateRequestFn → non-zero rejects
      app.⎕FX'r←Auth req' 'r←~''secret''≡req.GetHeader''x-token''' ⍝ AuthenticateFn → non-zero fails
      app.⎕FX'r←BasicAuth req' 'r←~(req.UserID req.Password)≡''admin'' ''pw''' ⍝ AuthenticateFn using Basic creds
      app.⎕FX'AfterReq req' '''x-post''req.SetHeader''1''' ⍝ PostProcessFn (non-result)
    ⍝ REST method handlers (called monadically with the Request)
      app.⎕FX'r←Get req;n' 'n←⎕NS''''' 'n.method←''GET''' 'r←n'
      app.⎕FX'r←Post req;n' 'n←⎕NS''''' 'n.method←''POST''' 'r←n'
      app.⎕FX'r←handlePut req;n' 'n←⎕NS''''' 'n.method←''handlePut''' 'r←n'
    ∇

⍝ ─── helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Expect←{⍺:0⍴⊂'' ⋄ ,⊂⍵}
    Contains←{∨/⍺⍷⍵}
    Match←{(,⍺)≡,⍵}                          ⍝ equal, ignoring scalar-vs-1-element-vector
    LoggedMatch←{∨/∨/¨(⊂⍵)⍷¨⍺.Logged}

    ∇ j←NewServer paradigm
    ⍝ create (but don't start) a test server on its own port, in the given paradigm
      j←⎕NEW TJarvis
      j.Port←BasePort+PortsUsed←PortsUsed+1
      j.CodeLocation←App
      j.Paradigm←paradigm
      j.DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD←'debug'
      j.WaitTimeout←5000
      Servers,←j
    ∇

    ∇ StopAll;j;c
      :For j :In Servers
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}j.Stop ⋄ {}j.LDRC.Close j.ServerName ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      :For c :In Clients
          :Trap 0 ⋄ {}#.Jarvis.LDRC.Close c ⋄ :EndTrap
      :EndFor
      (Servers Clients)←⍬ ⍬
    ∇

    ∇ c←j SendRaw text;rc
      (rc c)←2↑j.LDRC.Clt'' 'localhost'j.Port'Text'
      'Could not connect'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨rc≠0
      Clients,←⊂c
      {}j.LDRC.Send c text
    ∇

    ∇ (status headers body)←j Do args;method;path;headers;body;req;c;data
    ⍝ args: method path [headers [body]]; headers is a vector of (name value) pairs
    ⍝ sends one request (Connection: close) and returns the parsed status, header matrix and body
      (method path headers body)←4↑args,(≢args)↓'' '' ⍬ ''
      req←method,' ',path,' HTTP/1.1',CRLF,'Host: localhost',CRLF,'Connection: close',CRLF
      req,←∊{⍺,': ',⍵,CRLF}/¨headers
      req,←(method≢'GET')/'Content-Length: ',(⍕≢body),CRLF
      req,←CRLF,body
      c←j SendRaw req
      (status headers body)←ParseResponse j ReadAll(c 4000)
    ∇

    ∇ data←j ReadAll(c ms);end;w;rc;evt
    ⍝ read until the server closes the connection (or ms pass)
      data←'' ⋄ end←ms+⎕AI[3]
      :While ⎕AI[3]<end
          w←4↑(j.LDRC.Wait c 200),4⍴⊂''
          (rc evt)←w[1 3]
          :If rc=0
              :If (⊂evt)∊'Block' 'BlockLast' ⋄ data,←4⊃w ⋄ :EndIf
              :If (⊂evt)∊'BlockLast' 'Closed' 'Error' ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
          :ElseIf rc≠100 ⋄ :Leave
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ (status headers body)←ParseResponse data;i;head;lines
      status←0 ⋄ headers←0 2⍴⊂'' ⋄ body←''
      →0⍴⍨0∊⍴i←⍸(CRLF,CRLF)⍷data
      head←(¯1+⊃i)↑data
      body←(3+⊃i)↓data
      lines←{⍵~⎕UCS 13}¨(head≠⎕UCS 10)⊆head
      status←⊃(//)⎕VFI 2⊃' '(≠⊆⊢)⊃lines
      headers←↑{i←⍵⍳':' ⋄ (⎕C(i-1)↑⍵)({⍵↓⍨+/∧\' '=⍵}i↓⍵)}¨1↓lines
    ∇

    ∇ r←headers Header name
      r←(headers[;1]⍳⊂⎕C name)⊃headers[;2],⊂''
    ∇

    JSONhdr←⊂'Content-Type' 'application/json'

⍝ ─── JSON paradigm tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_JSONRoundTrip;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ a POST with a JSON body reaches the endpoint and the result comes back as JSON
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/add'JSONhdr'[1,2,3]'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'POST /add status ',⍕status
      r,←('6'Match body)Expect'POST /add body ',(⍕body),', expected 6'
      r,←('application/json'Contains headers Header'content-type')Expect'content-type ',headers Header'content-type'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/echo'JSONhdr'{"a":1,"b":[2,3]}'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'POST /echo status ',⍕status
      r,←(('"a"'Contains body)∧'"b"'Contains body)Expect'POST /echo should echo the object; got ',body
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_RequestAsLeftArg;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ an ambivalent endpoint receives the Request as its left argument
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/withreq'JSONhdr'[10,20]'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'status ',⍕status
      r,←('"post"'Contains body)Expect'endpoint should see req.Method (lower-cased) =post; got ',body
      r,←('30'Contains body)Expect'endpoint should see the payload (sum 30); got ',body
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_NotFound;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ an unknown function, and a hook function, both give 404
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.AuthenticateFn←'Auth'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/nosuchfn'(JSONhdr,⊂'x-token' 'secret')
      r,←(status=404)Expect'unknown function status ',⍕status
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/Auth'(JSONhdr,⊂'x-token' 'secret')
      r,←(status=404)Expect'calling a hook function should be 404; got ',⍕status
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_IncludeExclude;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ IncludeFns restricts the callable endpoints; ExcludeFns hides them
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.IncludeFns←'echo'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      r,←(200=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'JSONhdr'1')Expect'IncludeFns: /echo should be 200'
      r,←(404=⊃j Do'POST' '/add'JSONhdr'[1,2]')Expect'IncludeFns: /add should be 404'
      {}j.Stop
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.ExcludeFns←'secret'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed (exclude)'
      r,←(404=⊃j Do'POST' '/secret'JSONhdr'1')Expect'ExcludeFns: /secret should be 404'
      r,←(200=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'JSONhdr'1')Expect'ExcludeFns: /echo should be 200'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_ContentTypeChecks;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ a POST with no Content-Type, or a non-JSON Content-Type, is rejected with 400
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      r,←(400=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'⍬'123')Expect'POST with no Content-Type should be 400'
      r,←(400=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'(,⊂'Content-Type' 'text/plain')'123')Expect'POST text/plain should be 400'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_AllowGETs;j
    ⍝ GETs are refused unless AllowGETs is set
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.HTMLInterface←0 ⍝ so a GET isn't served the HTML interface
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      r,←(405=⊃j Do'GET' '/echo'⍬)Expect'GET with AllowGETs=0 should be 405'
      {}j.Stop
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.(HTMLInterface AllowGETs)←0 1
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r,←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed (AllowGETs)'
      r,←(200=⊃j Do'GET' '/echo'⍬)Expect'GET /echo with AllowGETs=1 should be 200'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Error500;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ an error in an endpoint gives 500, with the error name when ErrorInfoLevel≥1
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/boom'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←(status=500)Expect'POST /boom status ',⍕status
    ∇

⍝ ─── hook tests ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_AppInitClose;j
    ⍝ AppInitFn runs at Start, AppCloseFn runs at Stop
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.(AppInitFn AppCloseFn)←'Init' 'Closed'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      r,←(1=App.Inited)Expect'AppInitFn should have run at Start'
      {}j.Stop
      r,←(1=App.ClosedFlag)Expect'AppCloseFn should have run at Stop'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Validate;j
    ⍝ ValidateRequestFn rejects a request with 400
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.ValidateRequestFn←'Validate'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      r,←(400=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'(JSONhdr,⊂'x-validate' 'block')'1')Expect'a blocked request should be 400'
      r,←(200=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'JSONhdr'1')Expect'an accepted request should be 200'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_Authenticate;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ AuthenticateFn: a bad/absent token gives 401 with a WWW-Authenticate header; a good token gives 200
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.AuthenticateFn←'Auth'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/echo'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←(status=401)Expect'no token should be 401; got ',⍕status
      r,←(~0∊⍴headers Header'www-authenticate')Expect'401 should include a WWW-Authenticate header'
      r,←(200=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'(JSONhdr,⊂'x-token' 'secret')'1')Expect'a valid token should be 200'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_BasicAuth;j;tok;dummy
    ⍝ HTTP Basic credentials are decoded into UserID/Password for AuthenticateFn
      r←⍬
      dummy←⎕NEW #.Jarvis.Request
      tok←'Basic ',dummy.Base64Encode'admin:pw'
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.AuthenticateFn←'BasicAuth'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      r,←(200=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'(JSONhdr,⊂'Authorization'tok)'1')Expect'correct Basic credentials should be 200'
      r,←(401=⊃j Do'POST' '/echo'(JSONhdr,⊂'Authorization'('Basic ',dummy.Base64Encode'admin:wrong'))'1')Expect'wrong Basic credentials should be 401'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_PostProcess;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ PostProcessFn runs after the endpoint and can modify the response
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      j.PostProcessFn←'AfterReq'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/echo'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'status ',⍕status
      r,←('1'Match headers Header'x-post')Expect'PostProcessFn should add x-post header; got ',⍕headers Header'x-post'
    ∇

⍝ ─── REST paradigm tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_RESTDispatch;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ in REST mode the HTTP method selects the handler function; an unlisted method gives 405
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'REST'
      j.RESTMethods←'Get,Post'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'GET' '/'⍬
      r,←(status=200)Expect'GET status ',⍕status
      r,←('"GET"'Contains body)Expect'GET should call Get; got ',body
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←('"POST"'Contains body)Expect'POST should call Post; got ',body
      r,←(405=⊃j Do'PUT' '/'JSONhdr'1')Expect'PUT (not in RESTMethods) should be 405'
    ∇

    ∇ r←test_RESTCustomHandler;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ RESTMethods can map a method to a differently-named handler function
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'REST'
      j.RESTMethods←'Get,put/handlePut'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'PUT' '/'JSONhdr'1'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'PUT status ',⍕status
      r,←('"handlePut"'Contains body)Expect'PUT should call handlePut; got ',body
    ∇

⍝ ─── CORS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←test_CORS;j;status;headers;body
    ⍝ a cross-origin request gets Access-Control-Allow-Origin; a preflight gets 204
      r←⍬
      j←NewServer'JSON'
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴r←(0=⊃j.Start)Expect'Start failed'
      (status headers body)←j Do'POST' '/echo'(JSONhdr,⊂'Origin' 'http://example.com')'1'
      r,←(status=200)Expect'CORS POST status ',⍕status
      r,←('*'Match headers Header'access-control-allow-origin')Expect'CORS POST should reflect/allow origin; got ',⍕headers Header'access-control-allow-origin'
      (status headers body)←j Do'OPTIONS' '/echo'(('Origin' 'http://example.com')('Access-Control-Request-Method' 'POST'))
      r,←(status=204)Expect'CORS preflight status ',(⍕status),', expected 204'
      r,←(~0∊⍴headers Header'access-control-allow-origin')Expect'preflight should include Access-Control-Allow-Origin'
    ∇

:EndNamespace
